# Build intermediates.
# Source/Directory.Build.props sends them outside the mod folder: they must never end up in it,
# since RimWorld's Workshop uploader sends Mod/ as it stands, with no exclusion possible, and an
# obj/ sitting there would ship the publicised Assembly-CSharp.dll to every subscriber.
.build/
Source/obj/
Source/bin/

# Development environments
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.csproj.user

# Claude Code session worktrees and local settings. A session creates its worktree in the
# current directory, so sometimes inside this one, and each is a full copy of the repository.
# Until this folder became a repository of its own the rule lived in the monorepo's .gitignore,
# a file this repository does not carry.
.claude/

# Windows shortcuts dropped in the mod folder, never content.
*.lnk

# Pre-converted textures. RimWorld builds its own .dds cache beside every PNG it loads, so these
# appear inside Mod/Textures without anyone asking. They are derived files: they bloat the
# repository, they go stale the moment the PNG changes, and the game regenerates them. None exists
# here today - this mod ships no texture of its own - and the rule is here so none ever lands.
*.dds

# Pickle run evidence, kept on disk and never in git. Screenshots and Player.log grow without
# bound (PickleTools has seen 10 GB in a day), so the report itself stays out of the history and
# only a short text summary under docs/runs/ is committed, cited by STATUS.md. See the evidence
# section of TESTING.md for what is worth keeping out of a run and what is deleted with it.
Tests/Pickle/Evidence/
evidence/
pickle-reports-archive/
